.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt NIGHTSAVER.TOML 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nightsaver.toml
.Nd nightsaver configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Xr nightsaver 1
daemon reads its configuration from a TOML file.
The default location is
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nightsaver/config.toml ,
or
.Pa ~/.config/nightsaver/config.toml
if
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset or empty.
Another file may be named with
.Fl Fl config ;
that file must exist.
A missing default file is not an error.
An annotated sample is installed as
.Pa /usr/local/etc/nightsaver.toml.sample .
.Pp
Every key is optional.
Keys at the top level are given first, followed by the
.Sy [dpms]
and
.Sy [oled]
tables.
.Ss Precedence
Each setting is taken from the first of these that provides it:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
the command line,
.It
this file,
.It
the user's
.Pa ~/.xscreensaver ,
.It
the built-in default.
.El
.Pp
The files are checked for changes every five seconds and reloaded on
.Dv SIGHUP .
If the new contents cannot be parsed, the old settings are kept.
Unknown keys are ignored by the TOML parser; an invalid value or an invalid
.Va mode
rejects the whole file.
.Ss Durations
Keys of type
.Em duration
accept an integer number of seconds
.Pq Li 300
or a string:
.Li "300" ,
.Li "5:00"
(minutes:seconds) or
.Li "0:05:00"
(hours:minutes:seconds).
Negative values are rejected.
.Sh KEYS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va display No (string, default Dv $DISPLAY )
X display to manage.
.It Va verbose No (integer, default 0)
Log verbosity: 0 warnings, 1 info, 2 debug, 3 and above trace.
.It Va log_file No (string, default none)
Also append log lines to this file.
.It Va splash No (boolean, default false)
Accepted for compatibility; nightsaver has no splash screen.
.It Va timeout No (duration, default 0:10:00)
Idle time before the screen is blanked.
.It Va cycle No (duration, default 0:10:00)
Time between pattern changes.
.It Va lock No (boolean, default false)
Lock the screen when it is blanked.
.It Va lock_timeout No (duration, default 0:00:00)
Time after blanking before the screen becomes locked.
.It Va passwd_timeout No (duration, default 0:00:30)
How long the unlock dialog stays up without input.
.It Va pam_service No (string, default Qq xscreensaver )
PAM service name used to authenticate.
If the default policy does not exist in
.Pa /etc/pam.d
or
.Pa /usr/local/etc/pam.d
but a
.Qq nightsaver
policy does (installed by
.Ql make install-pam ) ,
that one is used automatically.
Any other name is used as given.
.It Va mode No (string, default Qq random )
Pattern selection:
.Qq one
shows only the pattern at index
.Va selected ;
.Qq random
changes between the patterns in
.Va patterns ;
.Qq random-same
is accepted and treated as
.Qq random ;
.Qq blank
shows pure black;
.Qq off
never activates.
Any other value is an error.
.It Va patterns No (array of strings, default Qq clock , Qq starfield , Qq matrix , Qq midnight , Qq cat , Qq juggler , Qq puppy , Qq penguin )
The pattern list.
An empty array is ignored.
Names are:
.Bl -tag -width starfield -compact
.It blank
Pure black.
.It clock
A time display that drifts slowly around the screen.
.It starfield
Stars flying outward.
.It matrix
Falling character rain.
.It midnight
The MidnightBSD logo as a drifting outline with a twinkling fill, and the
boot loader's ASCII brand beneath it.
.It cat
An ASCII-art cat that blinks, swishes its tail, naps and watches the odd mouse.
.It juggler
An ASCII-art stick figure juggling a three-ball cascade.
.It puppy
An ASCII-art puppy that wags its tail, pants, barks, gets excited when a
ball bounces past and naps.
.It penguin
An ASCII-art penguin that waddles back and forth in light snow, flaps its
flippers, perks up when a fish leaps past and naps standing up.
.El
.Pp
Also accepted as aliases:
.Qq stars ,
.Qq glmatrix
and
.Qq xmatrix .
.It Va selected No (integer, default 0)
Zero-based index into
.Va patterns ,
used when
.Va mode
is
.Qq one .
Clamped to the list.
.It Va fps No (integer, default 30)
Frame rate of animated patterns, limited to 1..120.
.It Va motion_threshold_px No (integer, default 10)
Cumulative pointer movement, in pixels, that wakes a blanked, unlocked screen.
.El
.Ss The [dpms] table
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va enabled No (boolean, default false)
Manage monitor power saving while blanked.
.It Va standby No (duration, default 2:00:00)
.It Va suspend No (duration, default 2:00:00)
.It Va off No (duration, default 4:00:00)
DPMS timeouts installed while the screen is blanked.
The server's previous settings are restored on unblanking.
.It Va quick_off No (boolean, default false)
Power the monitor off immediately when blanking.
.El
.Pp
On an X server without the DPMS extension the screen turns pure black instead
of powering off: after the shortest non-zero timeout above, or immediately with
.Va quick_off .
See
.Xr nightsaver 1 .
.Ss The [oled] table
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va max_brightness No (float, default 0.35)
Luma cap from 0.0 to 1.0 applied to every frame of every pattern.
The blank pattern is true black regardless.
.It Va shift_interval No (duration, default 0:01:00)
How often the whole frame is moved to a new position.
.It Va shift_max_px No (integer, default 16)
Maximum shift in pixels from the original position.
.It Va rest_interval No (duration, default 0:10:00)
How often a full-black rest interlude begins.
.It Va rest_duration No (duration, default 0:00:20)
How long each rest interlude lasts.
.It Va lit_budget No (float, default 0.05)
Target fraction of lit pixels, 0.0 to 1.0.
This is a hint passed to the patterns, not a hard limit.
.El
.Sh OLED PROTECTION
OLED panels age in proportion to how long and how brightly each pixel is lit.
All drawing therefore goes through a post-processing stage:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Va max_brightness
limits the brightness of the brightest pixel, at the cost of a dimmer
display.
.It
Pixel shift: every
.Va shift_interval
the whole picture takes a slow pseudo-random step, never more than
.Va shift_max_px
pixels from its origin, so no pixel stays at the edge of a shape.
.It
Rest interlude: every
.Va rest_interval
the screen goes entirely black for
.Va rest_duration ,
so each pixel gets a recovery period.
.It
Lit budget: each pattern is told how large a fraction of the screen it may
light, and draws sparse content on a black background.
.It
No static element persists: the clock drifts and the unlock dialog hides
itself after
.Va passwd_timeout .
.El
.Pp
For the best protection use
.Qq blank
mode, and enable
.Va dpms.enabled
with
.Va dpms.quick_off
so that the panel is switched off.
.Sh XSCREENSAVER COMPATIBILITY
If
.Pa ~/.xscreensaver
exists, these resources are read.
Names are matched case-insensitively and may carry the usual
.Li xscreensaver\&. ,
.Li XScreenSaver* ,
or
.Li *
prefix.
.Bl -tag -width ".Va dpmsQuickOff"
.It Va timeout , cycle , lock , lockTimeout , passwdTimeout
Mapped to the keys of the same name.
.It Va dpmsEnabled , dpmsStandby , dpmsSuspend , dpmsOff
Mapped to the
.Sy [dpms]
table.
.It Va dpmsQuickOff
Also
.Va dpmsQuickoffEnabled .
Mapped to
.Va dpms.quick_off .
.It Va mode
.Li one ,
.Li random ,
.Li random-same
(treated as random),
.Li blank
and
.Li off .
.It Va selected
Index into the full
.Va programs
list (zero-based), re-mapped onto the pattern list.
.It Va programs
Only the first word of each entry (the hack name) is used.
Entries that are disabled with a leading
.Li -
or whose name is not a nightsaver pattern are skipped.
The names
.Li blank ,
.Li clock ,
.Li starfield ,
.Li stars ,
.Li matrix ,
.Li glmatrix ,
.Li midnight ,
.Li midnightbsd ,
.Li logo ,
.Li cat ,
.Li asciicat ,
.Li kitty ,
.Li juggler ,
.Li juggle ,
.Li puppy ,
.Li dog ,
.Li puppydog ,
.Li penguin ,
.Li penguins
and
.Li xmatrix
are recognised.
If none match, the built-in list is kept.
.It Va verbose , splash
Boolean values.
.El
.Pp
Values written as
.Li fade
and
.Li unfade
are parsed but have no effect.
All other resources, including hack options, visual settings and
.Va lockVTs ,
are ignored.
Unparsable values are skipped with a warning in the log.
Durations in
.Pa ~/.xscreensaver
use
.Li H:MM:SS ,
.Li MM:SS
or seconds.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/nightsaver/config.toml
.It Pa ~/.xscreensaver
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/nightsaver.toml.sample
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A locking, mostly black configuration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
timeout = "0:05:00"
lock = true
lock_timeout = "0:00:30"
mode = "one"
patterns = ["clock"]

[dpms]
enabled = true
quick_off = true

[oled]
max_brightness = 0.25
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nightsaver 1 ,
.Xr nightsaver-command 1 ,
.Xr xscreensaver 1
